rem Quadtree Encoding (a simple
rem compression algorithm)
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=287
rem Find the length of the minimal
rem quadtree sequence of the black disk
rem D(N): the pixels of a 2^N square
rem with (x - 2^(N-1))^2 + (y -
rem 2^(N-1))^2 <= 2^(2N-2)

use numbers
use io
use cli

arg N integer = 24

rem A region that is all black or all
rem white costs 2 bits, any other 1 bit
rem and the cost of its four quarters.
rem Walk the quarters depth first,
rem keeping the open regions on a stack
rem of corner and size.
C = 2 ** (N - 1)
R2 = C * C
Cap = 4 * N + 8
Xs = array shape Cap fill 0
Ys = array shape Cap fill 0
Ss = array shape Cap fill 0
Ss 0 = 2 * C
Top = 1
rem A full quadtree with I internal
rem nodes has 3 * I + 1 leaves, so its
rem encoding costs 2 + 7 * I bits.
rem Mixed 2 by 2 squares need no walk
rem through their four pixel children.
Splits = 0
for
  if Top equal 0
    break
  end
  Top -= 1
  X0 = Xs Top
  Y0 = Ys Top
  S = Ss Top
  rem Exchange of x and y preserves
  rem the image: visit only one half.
  if X0 greater Y0
    continue
  end
  X1 = X0 + S - 1
  Y1 = Y0 + S - 1
  Fx = (X0 - C) * (X0 - C)
  Gx = (X1 - C) * (X1 - C)
  Far = Fx
  if Gx greater Far
    Far = Gx
  end
  Fy = (Y0 - C) * (Y0 - C)
  Gy = (Y1 - C) * (Y1 - C)
  Fary = Fy
  if Gy greater Fary
    Fary = Gy
  end
  Nx = C
  if C less X0
    Nx = X0
  end
  if C greater X1
    Nx = X1
  end
  Ny = C
  if C less Y0
    Ny = Y0
  end
  if C greater Y1
    Ny = Y1
  end
  Dx = Nx - C
  Dy = Ny - C
  Near = Dx * Dx + Dy * Dy
  Dark = Far + Fary at most R2
  if Dark or Near greater R2
    continue
  end
  Splits += 1
  if X0 less Y0
    Splits += 1
  end
  if S greater 2
    H = S // 2
    Xs Top = X0
    Ys Top = Y0
    Ss Top = H
    Xs (Top + 1) = X0 + H
    Ys (Top + 1) = Y0
    Ss (Top + 1) = H
    Xs (Top + 2) = X0
    Ys (Top + 2) = Y0 + H
    Ss (Top + 2) = H
    Xs (Top + 3) = X0 + H
    Ys (Top + 3) = Y0 + H
    Ss (Top + 3) = H
    Top += 4
  end
end
Answer = 2 + 7 * Splits
Answer print
